skip segwalrep/commit_blocking_on_standby a standby coordinator whose flush a commit waits for, as segwalrep/master_wal_switch; the isolation2 suite runs the test on a cluster with one (group mirrors4), and port/commit_blocking_on_standby_dml beside it
skip cancel_plpython a cancel that stops Python code (Cloudberry's cancel_pending_hook in PL/Python), which PostgreSQL 19's PL/Python has not: its busy loop and time.sleep() run on to the driver's timeout, in each pass
skip cancel_query the fault zlib_decompress_after_decompress_fn, which the ANALYZE of the zlib-compressed partition never reaches: its one row's column blocks gp_ao stores uncompressed, zlib not shortening blocks of gp_ao's format so small, where it shortens Cloudberry's longer datum stream blocks; it waits for it
